      "text": "System One models refer to a newly proposed class of specialized, lightweight neural models designed for fast, deterministic extraction and computation tasks — such as parsing, forecasting, or structured value estimation — from unstructured inputs. Contrasted with general-purpose System Two-style LLMs that perform open-ended reasoning, System One models prioritize low latency, high accuracy on narrow tasks, and cost efficiency, often deployed at the edge. The term was coined by TypeSafe and adopted by Cloudflare for its Clairic and Clef models, representing a shift toward modular, task-specific architectures in the AI stack."
