    "summary": "Cloudflare declared itself a \"neolab\" at the AI Engineer Code Summit, unveiling two System One models — Clef and Clairic — hosted on its Workers AI platform. The announcement positions Cloudflare alongside a new category of model builders distinct from OpenAI and Anthropic. Clairic, the first extraction model in this class, targets structured value retrieval from unstructured inputs with claims of higher accuracy, lower latency, and reduced cost versus general-purpose LLMs. The System One designation originated from TypeSafe a month earlier and has quickly drawn industry attention. Cloudflare plans to open-weight Clairic soon, signaling a push toward specialized, efficient model architectures over monolithic foundations.",
